// No service, and no tools yet. Spawning a subagent is `Shim::summon` in the
// shim's own process — a subagent is a chat in this harness, not a process of
// its own — so the routes that do it belong in `crates/web`, where the process
// is, and a service declared here would have nothing to run. What this
// directory is for: the toggle (an enabled `subagent` is what turns the
// harness's `/api/subagent*` routes on), the tier table's home, and the tools
// an agent would call once spawning from a turn is ruled on.
pub fn manifest() {
    #{
        name: "subagent",
        description: "Child sessions for a task: spawn one, watch its trace, steer it mid-turn or cancel it. A role maps to a model tier, the parent's own model by default.",
    }
}
